{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers","id":1191615,"title":"Tiers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-04T07:26:51-08:00","id":1191615,"title":"Tiers?","content":"OK; I was just looking through TC Core for what it had to say about tiers, and character creation mentioned that every character must choose his tier. It then said \u201cFor more information on Tiers, see p.XX.\u201d Fair enough; this <i>is</i> a rough manuscript. But searching through the rest of the text for the word \u201ctier\u201d didn't turn up anything that this might refer to.<br /> <br /> So, what happened?<br /> <br /> As I understand them (mainly from the information provided in Scion Origin), the Tier concepts are:<br /> <br /> 1: regular humans<br /> 2: extraordinary humans<br /> 3: superhuman<br /> 4: transcendent<br /> <br /> There's little difference between 1 and 2 other than 2 allowing you to pick up special abilities (Gifts and Dramatic Editing for Talents; Aptitudes for Psions). Tier 3 nets you an improved Target number on your dice, meaning more successes for the same dice pool; it also lets stats go a dot or two beyond 5. <br /> <br /> We know nothing about Tier 4 yet. I'm guessing that most Novas are Tier 3, and that Tier 4 \u201cNovas\u201d are the guys with the power to create universes et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-04-2018, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T22:56:18-08:00","id":1192153,"title":"","content":"The table for the tiers is on the 3rd page of chapter 3 in the preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23977-riainb","name":"RIainB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T00:27:12-08:00","id":1192165,"title":"","content":"Using 1e and 2e as a basis I'd say the following for Eximorphs(Novas, Aberrants etc)<br /> <br /> Tier 2: Stalwarts, Level one and Two Quantum powers.<br /> Tier 3: Novas, Level Three and Four powers.<br /> Tier 4: Novas, Level Five and Six Powers<br /> <br /> For Psychomorphs:<br /> Tier 2: Psions, Psiads, Mesmerists(levels 1-5 aptitudes and psychic knacks)<br /> Tier 3: Proxy powers(as seen in the new Aeon book)<br /> Tier 4: Who knows?<br /> <br /> And Paramorphs:<br /> Tier 2: Talents, Daredevils<br /> Tier 3: Max<br /> Tier 4: Unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:01:22-08:00","id":1192239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RIainB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192153#post1192153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The table for the tiers is on the 3rd page of chapter 3 in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda sorta. There's no mention of \u201cTier 1\u201d, \u201cTier 2\u201d, etc., which clashes with \u00c6on's use of those terms; and it implies (but does not say) that Talents are on a tier above Mundane but below Psion. As well, the only effect of Tier that is mentioned is the target number; just as one <i>could</i> interpret the table as expressing six tiers (Mundane, Talent, Psion, Proxy, Nova, Aberrant), one could also interpret it as only having two (Mundane/Talent/Psion, Proxy/Nova/Aberrant). This makes sense because the table in question isn't part of a \u201cTiers\u201d section; it's part of the \u201cTarget Numbers and Counting Successes\u201d section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:09:32-08:00","id":1192242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192165#post1192165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using 1e and 2e as a basis I'd say the following for Eximorphs(Novas, Aberrants etc)<br /> <br /> Tier 2: Stalwarts, Level one and Two Quantum powers.<br /> Tier 3: Novas, Level Three and Four powers.<br /> Tier 4: Novas, Level Five and Six Powers<br /> <br /> For Psychomorphs:<br /> Tier 2: Psions, Psiads, Mesmerists(levels 1-5 aptitudes and psychic knacks)<br /> Tier 3: Proxy powers(as seen in the new Aeon book)<br /> Tier 4: Who knows?<br /> <br /> And Paramorphs:<br /> Tier 2: Talents, Daredevils<br /> Tier 3: Max<br /> Tier 4: Unknown.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Eximorphs, don't forget Superiors. <br /> Also, I don't know that I'd classify Level 1 and 2 Quantum Powers as Tier 2: the common thread between Stalwarts and Superiors is that they don't have <i>any</i> Quantum Powers: everything takes the form of attribute improvements. I'd put Level 1\u20133 Quantum Powers on Tier 3, and Level 4\u20136 Quantum Powers on Tier 4. <br /> <br /> We've been told that Proxies aren't the only Tier 3 psychomorphs. If we include alien races in the mix, I'd say that the Doyen are Tier 3, and the \u201cbeings of pure thought\u201d that the Doyen would like to evolve into are Tier 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-06-2018, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T07:40:04-08:00","id":1192255,"title":"","content":"Paramorphs<br /> Tier 2: Talents &amp; Daredevils<br /> Tier 3: ???<br /> Tier 4: Max Mercer (Time Travel via dramatic editing seems like a T4 power)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:35:54-08:00","id":1192291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192255#post1192255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paramorphs<br /> Tier 2: Talents &amp; Daredevils<br /> Tier 3: ???<br /> Tier 4: Max Mercer (Time Travel via dramatic editing seems like a T4 power)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is assuming that Mercer is at all in control of his travel. If we look at it as something happening <i>to </i>him rather than something he's <i>doing</i>, it looks a lot less like a &quot;power.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T09:49:38-08:00","id":1192299,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Max does appear to have some sort of time manipulation ability; though from the 1e fiction, it appears to deal more with adjusting the flow of time than with actual travel through time: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3129-topher\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3129\" data-vbnamecard=\"3129\">Topher</a> Gerkey suggests, the time travel appears to be more a matter of something that happens to him rather than something he does.<br /> <br /> I can see Max being Tier 3; but not Tier 4, any more than Dr. Primorius or S.K. are Tier 4. (As opposed to Divas Mal, who very well may have achieved Tier 4 in the Nova Age.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:02:49-08:00","id":1192358,"title":"","content":"My tier scale is a broad power base. As we have the most knowledge oddly of Eximorphs on the scales 2, 3, and 4 based on 1e work I'm building backwards.<br /> <br /> Tier 2 is something I consider to use One Punchman disaster levels to be a wolf level, a threat to a large group of people and with the right setup potentially more so but generally by themselves they aren't going to destroy a city. This is why I put quantum level 1 and 2 powers here. They match up in my mind about on par with Dynamic Knacks from Adventure! And I wouldn't have a problem giving some of the more subtle ones to Superiors and claiming its &quot;cybernetics&quot;<br /> <br /> Tier 3 is something I consider something a group of tier 2s should work to fight and potentially are &quot;I can smash a city hulk style&quot; This is why I put access to level 3 powers as what moves a Nova from tier 2 to Tier 3. They have to use OPM Tiger level potential. I feel level 4 quantum powers still are within the Dangerous on a city scale but not explicitly regional so Demon level potential of danger.<br /> <br /> Level 5 Quantum powers are at the VERY least regionally dangerous and at the extreme end world endangering. They are to use OPM scales Dragon tipping into God scale. At the very least they are natural disasters on par with a hurricane, and can scale up to being a threat to all of humanity on a single planet just by using one power.<br /> <br /> Level 6 Quantum powers start at Deathstar Laser level and move up to Create yourown universe(who in turn makes theirown universe and so on and so on). It starts at World ending threat or God scale disaster and moves into what I call &quot;Rick Sanchez&quot; scale(the potential to destroy galactic civilizations and or universes!)<br /> <br /> So that's how I see the scale of Eximorphs. I'm not as clear how to handle Mega attributes, since they are matter of quantity rather than a qualitative difference. I'm also ignoring Time Travel stuff for this scale, since all time Travel might be crosstime travel now in the new edition(more on this when talking paramorphs)<br /> <br /> So Psychomorphs!<br /> <br /> What we have so far psychic knacks and everything 1-5 puts you roughly in tier 2 as a power though enough Tier 2 stuff can kick you into tier 3.<br /> <br /> Right now we have proxy tier psychics, Proxies and I am going to say doyen in the tier 3 psychomorph category. Doyen do not demonstrate any qualitative upgrade in power over proxies EXCEPT having a backdoor hack into all psions. This isn't though an innate power of the Doyen but rather a security flaw in the Prometheus chambers, so they mostly have the same potential as Tier 3s but with some greater versatility.<br /> <br /> As there are powers that I don't think are &quot;tier 4&quot; scale that seem to currently be beyond individuals(shaping other people for example) I imagine there is another level of power before hitting tier 4.. what would be on par with Nova level 4 quantum powers.<br /> <br /> So what does Tier 4 Psychic powers look like? Entire perfect psychic hive mind gestalts that give up no level of individuality, immortal psychic ghosts, Teleporting planets, shaping whole species, lighting Jovian gas giants into Stars. <br /> <br /> Finally Paramorphs.<br /> <br /> We have only mechanical examples of Tier 2 characters, daredevils and Talents, the same thing really just different editions. However we do have some idea what a Tier 3 should look like with Max as all the Hammersmith characters got kicked to Tier 3.We also have some idea of how Paramorph powers work by connecting you to alternative realities.<br /> <br /> So in 1e Max demonstrating some control over his own personal passage of time along with the ability to jump to important points in history. I would comment these important points all seem to have Flux based accidents perhaps with some Quantum or Psi in the mix but generally some major event that has strong Flux would be a place he could show up(N-day, the Aberrant War, Aeon era etc). 1e seemed to vary between whether he could change history or whether he was in already a part of the events, with 2e I'm going to consider the fact that he may not actually be capable of true time travel but rather cross time travel. That is he can travel to these various points but they are separate time lines, he can potentially shape the future based on what he saw happen in another world but that world will always be there. Other powers might have some equivalent of time manipulation but time manipulation and cross time travel comes easiest to the Paramorph.<br /> <br /> Other powers the Potential tier 3 paramorph might have would be extreme levels of entropy/fate to use mage terms to be able to actively manipulate probability along with time<br /> <br /> The final form I can imagine for Paramorph powers would be something akin to more extreme charms in exalted, people who are just &quot;so good&quot; at a field they can play too. If Mr. fantastic is a Nova with mega int, tony Stark would be the Talent with super skill, batman would also obviously apply. More these types may in fact scale based on conflict(this really explains batman rather well)<br /> <br /> With this in mind I have no idea what a Tier 4 Paramorph might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:17:25-08:00","id":1192362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192291#post1192291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is assuming that Mercer is at all in control of his travel. If we look at it as something happening <i>to </i>him rather than something he's <i>doing</i>, it looks a lot less like a &amp;quot;power.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In support of what Topher said, I'd suggest that Max's time travel probably functions a lot like dramatic editing, where it's something the character does but their 'player' is the one with any real control over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:42:07-08:00","id":1192403,"title":"","content":"Be careful not to conflate Tier with Scale: I'm pretty sure what you're saying about Wolf/Tiger/Dragon/God is a matter of Scale, not Tier. (What exactly is the difference between Scale and Tier? That's something I'd like clarified \u2014 which is why the absence of the referenced \u201cTiers\u201d section bothers me so much.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:03:21-08:00","id":1192410,"title":"","content":"I think Max, Michael, and Sara, thanks to their proximity to the Hammersmith event, started at Tier 3 while everyone else was Tier 2 in the Adventure! Era.<br /> <br /> With their temporally linear progression, Divis and S.K. are Tier 4 by the Aberrant era. By the Aeon Era,<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> S.K. has been knocked back down to Tier 3 by Doyen meddling (when she was turned into a Psion), </div></div> </div> </div> while Divis has progressed to something unknown and exited known reality.<br /> <br /> It is possible to encounter Tier 3 or Tier 4 Max at any point in time. Tier 3 can\u2019t control his temporal movement and is just trying to use the knowledge he has of the future to put others on the right path in the window of time he has in any given era, and learn as much as he can to use after his next temporal shift. Tier 4 Max, from later in his own timeline has reached an equilibrium with time and seems to have complete understanding of his relationship with the timestream, which plays out similarly though not identically to control. Understanding the bigger picture of time he is less interventionist than his earlier self and may act in ways that don\u2019t seem to make total sense at all without a bizarre butterfly map of causality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-06-2018, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T16:37:14-08:00","id":1192453,"title":"","content":"My understanding of Tier 4:<br /> <b>Eximorphs:</b> Darkseid, Galactus; Xavier-as-Onslaught. These are the entities who are to supers as supers are to ordinary people. Divas Mal never achieved that level. <br /> <b>Psychomorphs</b>: Star Trek's Organians, Q, and similar entities. The Doyen <i>wish</i> to achieve this state, but haven't. Neither has S.K.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Remember, the Doyen abuse S.K. limited her future potential; it did <i>not</i> remove any abilities she had already developed. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Paramorphs:</b> let's see what the Tier 3 ones look like before speculating on Tier 4. That said, Sam Beckett may have achieved Tier 4 at the end of <i>Quantum Leap</i>: it wouldn't surprise me if Tier 3 Paramorphs needed some sort of guide for time or cross-time travel, with Tier 4 getting unrestricted travel among other perks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-06-2018, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T17:14:17-08:00","id":1192468,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible that Mercer's situation is unique to him and no other Talent would be affected the same way. It might be that any Talent exposed to concentrated &quot;Z-Waves&quot; develops a completely unique weirdness, and his happens to be time-related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T17:39:57-08:00","id":1192477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192403#post1192403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be careful not to conflate Tier with Scale: I'm pretty sure what you're saying about Wolf/Tiger/Dragon/God is a matter of Scale, not Tier. (What exactly is the difference between Scale and Tier? That's something I'd like clarified \u2014 which is why the absence of the referenced \u201cTiers\u201d section bothers me so much.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought scale was more like fighting a Leviathan ship, or Godzilla... my tiers break down is just how i see the powers shaking out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192453#post1192453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of Tier 4:<br /> <b>Eximorphs:</b> Darkseid, Galactus; Xavier-as-Onslaught. These are the entities who are to supers as supers are to ordinary people. Divas Mal never achieved that level.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't generally feel Darkseid is Tier 4. Darkseid with the Antilife Equasion, yes but Standard New Gods seem about on Par with Superman, what I call &quot;upper 3&quot;(now Silver age superman or Superman 1 million, that's tier 4).<br /> <br /> Similarly Thanos is Tier 3, Thanos with the Infinity Gauntlet is Tier 4.<br /> <br /> I feel its more a matter of qualitative than just a matter of having &quot;MORE&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T17:42:20-08:00","id":1192478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192453#post1192453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of Tier 4:<br /> <b>Eximorphs:</b> Darkseid, Galactus; Xavier-as-Onslaught. These are the entities who are to supers as supers are to ordinary people. Divas Mal never achieved that level. <br /> <b>Psychomorphs</b>: Star Trek's Organians, Q, and similar entities. The Doyen <i>wish</i> to achieve this state, but haven't. Neither has S.K.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Remember, the Doyen abuse S.K. limited her future potential; it did <i>not</i> remove any abilities she had already developed. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Paramorphs:</b> let's see what the Tier 3 ones look like before speculating on Tier 4. That said, Sam Beckett may have achieved Tier 4 at the end of <i>Quantum Leap</i>: it wouldn't surprise me if Tier 3 Paramorphs needed some sort of guide for time or cross-time travel, with Tier 4 getting unrestricted travel among other perks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough - though the way Mal\u2019s actually presented in first edition does place him pretty far above any existent character, but as i\u2019m for that being toned down this edition, I don\u2019t object to him and SK just being high Tier 3 at that point.<br /> <br /> I stand by my idea of Maxwell\u2019s non-linear power curve meaning you can meet him completely adrift in time trying to grab a raft, or you can meet him as seeming temporal bodhissatva - it\u2019s just earlier and later in the story from his POV.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve had the idea before that Q has a whole arc where he actually matured from immature trickster looking to amuse himself, to teacher actually trying to enlighten Picard - it\u2019s just we were seeing said arc completely out of order from the perspective of linear humans (and co).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T23:17:56-08:00","id":1192528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192468#post1192468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible that Mercer's situation is unique to him and no other Talent would be affected the same way. It might be that any Talent exposed to concentrated &amp;quot;Z-Waves&amp;quot; develops a completely unique weirdness, and his happens to be time-related.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and no. We've been told outright that the secret behind Talents is that they use cross-time Flux subconsciously to bend the odds in their favor, and that this can also translate into the ability to influence time. Can it manifest in other ways? Probably \u2014 but those \u201cother ways\u201d should be able to tie back to Flux in some reasonably concise way. I could, for instance, see Tier 3 Paramorphs being able to travel to other dimensions (if they exist) or influencing space; but it would be too much to claim that a Tier 3 Paramorph could engage in, say, Hydrokinesis, or could transform herself into a wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T01:04:31-08:00","id":1192549,"title":"","content":"Talents don't have <i>powers</i>.Not even Dramatic Editing is a power, from an in-character perspective. If Talents were superhuman, they could be identified as not baseline human, and we know they can't be.Yeah? So any advanced weirdness around them has to be just that - in-character, it's happening <i>around</i> them. Or near them. Or to them.Just lucky, I guess (or unlucky)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T06:40:59-08:00","id":1192591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192549#post1192549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talents don't have <i>powers</i>.Not even Dramatic Editing is a power, from an in-character perspective. If Talents were superhuman, they could be identified as not baseline human, and we know they can't be.Yeah? So any advanced weirdness around them has to be just that - in-character, it's happening <i>around</i> them. Or near them. Or to them.Just lucky, I guess (or unlucky)!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> We know its difficult for them to be identified but there are some indications that the situation has been observed both at Aeon and with clairsentients. I mean in the 22nd century they aren't sure Psiads exist either.<br /> <br /> <br /> That being said something that is to Talents are Psiads are to Psions might be interesting.<br /> <br /> And the Transition to Tier 3 while apparently rather natural for Psychomorphs may be far more difficult for Paramorphs and Eximorphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:10:47-08:00","id":1192754,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m inclined to rip off Star Trek DS9 and have detecting and identifying Talents (possible but not yet accomplished in the 2120s) be a matter of observing the spin of sub-atomic particles. Under normal circumstances, wave form collapse results in a 50/50 split between clockwise and counter-clockwise spin. In the presence of Talents, or at least Talents spending Inspiration, the percentages are thrown wildly off by the warping of probability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:44:17-08:00","id":1192820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192754#post1192754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m inclined to rip off Star Trek DS9 and have detecting and identifying Talents (possible but not yet accomplished in the 2120s) be a matter of observing the spin of sub-atomic particles. Under normal circumstances, wave form collapse results in a 50/50 split between clockwise and counter-clockwise spin. In the presence of Talents, or at least Talents spending Inspiration, the percentages are thrown wildly off by the warping of probability.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Aeon just had a complicated multiweek test that wasn't 100 percent, which is probably about right to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T16:32:59-08:00","id":1192842,"title":"","content":"My intention with Project Tantalus was that it was 100% guesswork and they have zero proof. The other Triton divisions don't quite think of them as trying to prove the existence of phlogiston, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T18:22:34-08:00","id":1192892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Topher Gerkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192842#post1192842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intention with Project Tantalus was that it was 100% guesswork and they have zero proof. The other Triton divisions don't quite think of them as trying to prove the existence of phlogiston, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. They're working backwards. Due to the Hammersmith event, they know powerful psychomorphs and less-powerful psychomorphs exist. They know powerful eximorphs and less-powerful eximorphs exist. They know Max Mercer exists, so.... where are the &quot;little&quot; paramorphs? What do they look like? How would we identify them?<br /> <br /> Aeon looks for (and attracts) daring and skilled individuals simply by the nature of the organization. Just like Microsoft and Google attract creative, skilled coders and engineers. Most of Aeon doesn't find anything unusual about that. So when Tantalus points their fingers and insists there's something <i>special</i> about them beyond normal human skill and talent, their peers mostly roll their eyes and say &quot;sure, Frank.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, Tantalus <i>does</i> continue to get decent funding from the Aeon Council, so maybe they're on to something after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T18:48:56-08:00","id":1192898,"title":"","content":"So if &quot;Aberrants&quot; in the Aeon sense (the big ones, not the mutant minions) are Tier 4... but the Novas on Eden are not exponentially more powerful than the Nova-Age Novas - can we assume that &quot;Corruption&quot; (1E &quot;Taint&quot;) is the key to Eximorph evolution, and the Novas on Eden essentially hit a power ceiling because of tethering themselves to their own humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:08:00-08:00","id":1192912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192892#post1192892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much. They're working backwards. Due to the Hammersmith event, they know powerful psychomorphs and less-powerful psychomorphs exist. They know powerful eximorphs and less-powerful eximorphs exist. They know Max Mercer exists, so.... where are the &quot;little&quot; paramorphs? What do they look like? How would we identify them?<br /> <br /> Aeon looks for (and attracts) daring and skilled individuals simply by the nature of the organization. Just like Microsoft and Google attract creative, skilled coders and engineers. Most of Aeon doesn't find anything unusual about that. So when Tantalus points their fingers and insists there's something <i>special</i> about them beyond normal human skill and talent, their peers mostly roll their eyes and say &quot;sure, Frank.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, Tantalus <i>does</i> continue to get decent funding from the Aeon Council, so maybe they're on to something after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its a matter of either &quot;they are onto something&quot; or they have a good statistical backing for who the most compitent people are in various fields. Either way they have pretty good odds of telling you who should go on a mission.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T20:09:23-08:00","id":1192942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1191615-tiers?p=1192898#post1192898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if &quot;Aberrants&quot; in the Aeon sense (the big ones, not the mutant minions) are Tier 4... but the Novas on Eden are not exponentially more powerful than the Nova-Age Novas - can we assume that &quot;Corruption&quot; (1E &quot;Taint&quot;) is the key to Eximorph evolution, and the Novas on Eden essentially hit a power ceiling because of tethering themselves to their own humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>1e's Teragen featured techniques for channeling Taint in a \u201cproductive\u201d (read: less harmful) manner, allowing them to achieve greater levels of power before their Taint destroys them and eventually sparking a \u201csecond Eruption\u201d called a Chrysalis that \u201celevates\u201d them further. Tier 4? Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}